                adventureType_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:55:44.478-07:00"
                description="&lt;p>The road north from San Francisco follows the Pacific for most of a thousand kilometres. We ride the best of it in five stages of 70 to 100 kilometres, and a van carries bikes and riders over the stretches in between. Expect steady climbs, ocean wind and a clam chowder at the end of each day.&lt;/p>"
                description_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                description_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:55:44.477-07:00"
                difficulty="Intermediate"
                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:55:44.479-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>A road or touring bike in good order (hire is possible)&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Helmet, cycling clothes and a windproof, waterproof jacket&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Two water bottles and front and rear lights for the fog&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:55:44.481-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}12"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-27T14:50:17.035-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;h2>Days 1 and 2: Bridge, cliffs and redwoods&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>We roll out over the Golden Gate Bridge and follow the coast road north, high above the sea. On the second day the route turns inland through a forest of redwoods, on a quiet road where the trees stand close enough to touch.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Days 3 and 4: The Oregon coast&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>Across the state line the shore becomes a string of headlands, sea stacks and long empty beaches, with a lighthouse every few hours. We sleep in small harbour towns and eat what the boats bring in.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Day 5: Inland to Portland&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>The last stage leaves the sea and crosses the coastal hills through farmland and vineyards to Portland, where the trip ends with dinner in the city.&lt;/p>"
